The base set carries zstd, unzstd and zstdcat, and the man set their manual: zstd is imported into the base system.

The install sets are zstd archives and the installer extracts them with zstd -dc, so the
base system ships the program (usr/bin/file-tools/zstd, imported from its upstream at the
pin of its UPSTREAM.toml, BSD licence).

--- a/distrib/sets/lists/base/mi
+++ b/distrib/sets/lists/base/mi
@@ -710,6 +710,7 @@
 ./usr/bin/uniq
 ./usr/bin/units
 ./usr/bin/unvis
+./usr/bin/unzstd
 ./usr/bin/uptime
 ./usr/bin/usbhidaction
 ./usr/bin/usbhidctl
@@ -751,6 +752,8 @@
 ./usr/bin/zless
 ./usr/bin/zmore
 ./usr/bin/znew
+./usr/bin/zstd
+./usr/bin/zstdcat
 ./usr/games
